  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "HL functions extend SL content with the modulus function, rational functions with oblique asymptotes, and complex roots of polynomials.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Modulus (absolute value) function",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "\\[|f(x)|:\\text{ reflect negative part above }x\\text{-axis}.\\]\\[f(|x|):\\text{ reflect positive part across }y\\text{-axis}.\\]<p>Equations \\(|f(x)|=k\\) give two cases: \\(f(x)=k\\) and \\(f(x)=-k.\\) Inequalities \\(|f(x)|&lt;k\\) give \\(-k&lt;f(x)&lt;k.\\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Factor/remainder theorem (polynomials)",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p><strong>Complex conjugate root theorem:</strong> if \\(p(x)\\) has real coefficients and \\(a+bi\\) is a root, then \\(a-bi\\) is also a root.</p><p><strong>Relation between roots and coefficients</strong> for \\(az^3+bz^2+cz+d=0\\) with roots \\(\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma\\):</p>\\[\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma=-b/a,\\quad\\alpha\\beta+\\beta\\gamma+\\gamma\\alpha=c/a,\\quad\\alpha\\beta\\gamma=-d/a.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "workedExampleCard",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked Example 2.1",
          "ar": null
        },
        "problem": {
          "en": "Sketch \\(y=|2x-4|\\) and solve \\(|2x-4|=x+1.\\)",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "<p>V-shape with vertex at \\((2,0).\\)</p><p>Case 1: \\(2x-4=x+1\\Rightarrow x=5.\\) Check: \\(|6|=6=6.\\;\\checkmark\\)</p><p>Case 2: \\(2x-4=-(x+1)\\Rightarrow3x=3\\Rightarrow x=1.\\) Check: \\(|{-2}|=2=2.\\;\\checkmark\\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "workedExampleCard",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked Example 2.2 — Complex roots",
          "ar": null
        },
        "problem": {
          "en": "\\(p(x)=x^3-3x^2+7x-5\\) has root \\(x=1.\\) Find all roots.",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "<p>Factor out \\((x-1)\\): \\(p(x)=(x-1)(x^2-2x+5).\\)</p><p>Quadratic: \\(x=\\dfrac{2\\pm\\sqrt{4-20}}{2}=1\\pm2i.\\)</p><p>Roots: \\(x=1,\\;1+2i,\\;1-2i.\\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Modulus function",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( |f(x)| \\) reflects negative output above \\( x \\)-axis",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Odd/even symmetry",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "Odd: \\( f(-x)=-f(x) \\); Even: \\( f(-x)=f(x) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "warn",
        "label": {
          "en": "Practice Problem",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>\\(p(x)=x^4-2x^3+5x^2-8x+4\\) has \\(x=1\\) as a double root. Find all roots.</p><details style=\"margin-top:8px\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer;font-weight:600\">Show solution</summary><div style=\"margin-top:8px\"><p>\\((x-1)^2\\) divides \\(p(x)\\). Divide: \\(p(x)=(x-1)^2(x^2+4).\\)</p><p>\\(x^2+4=0\\Rightarrow x=\\pm2i.\\) Roots: \\(1\\) (double), \\(\\pm2i.\\)</p></div></details>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example-grid",
        "label": {
          "en": "Rational function sketch",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Sketch \\(f(x)=\\dfrac{2x^2-x-6}{x^2-4}\\), stating all asymptotes and intercepts.</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong> Factor: \\(f(x)=\\dfrac{(2x+3)(x-2)}{(x+2)(x-2)}=\\dfrac{2x+3}{x+2}\\) for \\(x\\neq2\\).</p><p>Vertical asymptote: \\(x=-2\\). Horizontal: \\(y\\to2\\). Hole at \\(x=2\\), \\(y=\\frac{7}{4}\\). \\(x\\)-int: \\(x=-\\frac{3}{2}\\). \\(y\\)-int: \\(y=\\frac{3}{2}\\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example-grid",
        "label": {
          "en": "Solving modulus equation",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Solve \\(|2x-3|=x+1\\).</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong> Case 1: \\(2x-3=x+1\\implies x=4\\). Check: \\(|5|=5\\). ✓</p><p>Case 2: \\(2x-3=-(x+1)\\implies 3x=2\\implies x=\\frac{2}{3}\\). Check: \\(|{-\\frac{5}{3}}|=\\frac{5}{3}=\\frac{2}{3}+1\\). ✓</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "<strong>Practice:</strong> Find the range of \\(f(x)=\\dfrac{x}{x^2+1}\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "Let \\(y=\\frac{x}{x^2+1}\\). Then \\(yx^2-x+y=0\\). For real \\(x\\): \\(\\Delta=1-4y^2\\geq0\\implies y\\in\\left[-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2}\\right]\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
